{"availability":"available","full":"SecurityRonin/cryptlab","name":"cryptlab","description":"CryptLab — crack classical ciphers yourself: Caesar, Vigenère & frequency analysis. Hands-on cryptography teaching tool.","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-11T01:13:11Z","updated":"2026-10-10T04:34:06Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cryptlab-ten.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://securityronin-cryptlab.netlify.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.859Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.859Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.859Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.859Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Make a cipher, then break one — the 1,200-year duel of codemakers and codebreakers, hands-on in your browser.","CryptLab is a teaching tool built as a timeline. The tabs run left to right in the order cryptanalysis was actually invented, and each technique is strictly stronger than the one before it:","Tabs ②, ④ and ⑤ work on the same ciphertext and the same board, so a student breaks one message with a thousand years of escalating technique and watches the score climb. Later tabs stay locked until the earlier one has been tried: pressing its main button unlocks the next tab at once, and so do any eight clicks spent working the board."],"features":["The rotor is not a toy approximation: fed all As from positions AAA it produces BDZGOWCXLTKSBTMCDLPBMUQOFXYHCX, the published Enigma I test vector, and that's asserted in the suite as an independent oracle rather than a…","There is no Shor mode, and the page says why: Shor is not a cipher. It's the only thing here with no encrypt side at all.","All 25 Caesar decryptions at once. You read them and pick the English one — no scores, no marked row, nothing pre-announced. The lesson isn't technique, it's that the keyspace is too small to matter.","Index of coincidence bars for key lengths 1–12. English clusters near 0.067, random near 0.038; you tap the shortest bar that reaches English.","The machine's opinion is opt-in. \"Score them for me\" and \"Mark the peak for me\" reveal the statistical answer after you've had a go — which is the actual teaching moment, since it shows a counter reaching by arithmetic…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SecurityRonin/cryptlab/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"94594bb76f95d4ba6f9b24b8c7a5231006cd37587695074a89c405f0fa32d2b3","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.971Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.971Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Make a cipher, then break one — the 1,200-year duel of codemakers and codebreakers, hands-on in your browser.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SecurityRonin/cryptlab/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"94594bb76f95d4ba6f9b24b8c7a5231006cd37587695074a89c405f0fa32d2b3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SecurityRonin/cryptlab/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.972Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T04:34:06Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/SecurityRonin/cryptlab/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T11:07:50.974Z","hash":"94594bb76f95d4ba6f9b24b8c7a5231006cd37587695074a89c405f0fa32d2b3","originalBytes":13543,"storedBytes":13543,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["one","letter","key","letters","rather","shor","caesar","english","pad","test","cipher","crib","message","web","which","cribs","each","pairs","playwright","read","rsa","same","search","short","tab","tool","vigen","what","against","board","drag","end","every","length","machine","npx","one-time","page","single","statistics","word","arithmetic","ciphertext","itself","keyword","lab","long","pair","random","real","run","score","tabs","technique","them","three","tools","why","actually","after","al-kindi","answer","bar","break","built","candidates","cannot"